tion":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":86.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.052259997,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":34.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.583,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":58.3,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"Barrett Business Services, Inc. provides business management solutions for small and mid-sized companies in the United States. It develops a management platform that integrates a knowledge-based approach from the management consulting industry with tools from the human resource outsourcing industry. The company also offers professional employer services under which it enters into a client services agreement to establish a co-employment relationship with each client company, assuming responsibility for payroll, payroll taxes, workers compensation coverage, and other administration functions for the client's existing workforce. In addition, it provides staffing and recruiting services, such as on-demand or short-term staffing assignment, contract staffing, direct placement, and long-term or indefinite-term on-site management services. The company serves customers in various industries, including construction, waste management and remediation services, manufacturing, transportation and warehousing, health care, leisure and hospitality, retail, professional and advisory services, and wholesale trade industries. Barrett Business Services, Inc. was incorporated in 1965 and is headquartered in Vancouver, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Gary Edward Kramer Jr. | President, CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 141K people. Revenue per employee of $9K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $333 of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $73 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 283\u00d7 revenue per employee (very high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Barrett Business Services, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $737M market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 89% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 81-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 20% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $47M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.21\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 5.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 24% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Shares offer a 27% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","19 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Industrials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding the Setup: (BBSI) and Scalable Risk","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/22/Understanding_the_Setup:_BBSI_and_Scalable_Risk_111026014602_1794293162.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794293162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Barrett Business Services, Inc. (BBSI) \u2013 What Are Brokerages Saying About This Stock?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/barrett-business-services-inc-bbsi-what-are-brokerages-saying-about-this-stock.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794129320.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.765,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Barrett Business (BBSI) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/barrett-business-bbsi-q3-2026-